## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical IAM policy construction tying S3 prefixes to service identities, a common beginner task for real-world isolation.

## Key Concepts
- IAM policies and bucket policies
- s3:prefix and path-based access control
- Least privilege and revocation testing
- Trust policy basics for role assumption

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus/*"]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus",
        "arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus/logs/${serviceName}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"s3:prefix": "logs/${serviceName}/"}
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus/logs/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce encryption at rest for these objects?
- How would you audit access attempts and detect violations?
- How would you handle new services joining without updating policies frequently?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to craft strict per-tenant isolation across multiple AWS accounts, combining STS-based role assumption, granular S3 bucket policies, KMS key rotation, and an auditable governance workflow. It also exercises incident response via quarantine and DynamoDB auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-account IAM roles and trust policies
- S3 bucket policies with prefix-scoped access
- AWS KMS CMK rotation and key policy implications
- Lambda-based policy enforcement and DynamoDB auditing
- Canary testing for tenancy violations and quarantine workflows

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::INGEST_ACCT_ID:role/TenantAppRole"},
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::telemetry-bucket/tenants/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption": "aws:kms"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      ""Action": ["kms:Encrypt","kms:Decrypt"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:REGION:ACCOUNT_ID:key/CMK_ID",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"kms:ViaService": "s3.REGION.amazonaws.com"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you automate tenant onboarding and rotation of CMKs per tenant? 
- How would you validate that no cross-tenant reads occur in Analytics using Athena views?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of end-to-end event-driven AWS patterns, from S3 events to Lambda processing to DynamoDB storage, with proper IAM scoping and TLS enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- S3 Event Notifications
- Lambda execution roles (least privilege)
- DynamoDB PutItem permissions
- S3 bucket policy TLS enforcement
- Security without public access and basic end-to-end testing

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::company-logs/app1/*"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["dynamodb:PutItem"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:REGION:ACCOUNT_ID:table/App1LogSummary"
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::company-logs/app1/*",
      "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "false"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate resilience against Lambda timeouts or large files?
- How would you extend this to multiple app prefixes with isolation rules?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical AWS multi-tenant isolation at scale, combining IAM session tags, Lake Formation, data catalog usage, and automated revocation; probes policy design, GitOps deployment, and testing.

## Key Concepts
- IAM role session tags
- Lake Formation permissions
- Data catalog integration
- Event-driven revocation with DynamoDB, EventBridge, Step Functions
- GitOps deployment of IAM policies
- Auditability: CloudTrail, Config, Access Analyzer

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy snippet (AssumeRole requires matching tenant-id tag)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      },
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/PrincipalRoleForTenant"}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Permission policy snippet (tenant-scoped S3 and Lake Formation actions)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["lakeformation:GetDataAccess"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"lakeformation:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross-tenant leakage with automated CI checks?
- What monitoring would you add to detect revocation failures and alert on latency breaches?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses advanced AWS ABAC, cross-account governance, and policy-as-code in a multi-tenant data lake; targets practical use of IAM Identity Center, PrincipalTags, Lake Formation, and a GitOps deployment flow.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with session/principal tags
- Lake Formation fine-grained permissions
- Cross-account policy deployment (GitOps)
- Revocation latency and audits (CloudTrail, Config, Access Analyzer)

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:saml-provider/AWS_SSO" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "tenant-A"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/tenant-A/*"
